+## Offline mode
+
+Settings → Offline mode downloads a small language model once (Qwen 2.5, about 0.5 GB or
+1.1 GB) and runs it on the phone with llama.cpp. No internet or API key is needed after that.
+
+- **Use the on-phone model only**: every reply comes from the phone. Nothing is sent to the cloud.
+- **Off (default)**: Oye uses your cloud providers first and switches to the phone model
+  when the internet or the keys fail, if the model is downloaded.
+
+The phone model is much smaller than cloud models: replies are simpler, it may ignore the
+JSON format (Oye then shows the plain text), and it is weaker in Urdu. Offline mode runs on
+64-bit ARM phones (arm64-v8a) only and needs a few GB of free RAM for the 1.5B model.
+
